# Line endings are decided here rather than by whoever cloned the repo.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so a checkout writes CRLF
# into the working tree while the blobs stay LF. Clients that do not read that setting then see
# every checked-out file as wholly rewritten, which buries a real diff under thousands of lines
# of nothing. Pinning it here settles it for every client, and matches end_of_line = lf in
# .editorconfig, which the autocrlf behaviour was quietly overriding.

# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and check it out as LF. That includes the
# .sln, which is already LF in the index and builds fine as LF -- singling it out for CRLF would
# change how the one file this project is fussiest about gets written, for no gain.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never examined for line endings, never diffed as text.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
